+//
+// Enabled only when DXMT_RECORD_DIR is set (and, if DXMT_RECORD_EXE is set, only
+// in that executable). The game then receives a pass-through device and
+// immediate context that forward every call to the real DXMT objects. Nothing
+// is written until a recording is triggered (Control-Command-B in game, or
+// DXMT_RECORD_START_FRAME); the recording then captures DXMT_RECORD_FRAMES frames:
+// every call, the data written through Map and UpdateSubresource, and the
+// contents of every pre-existing object at the moment it is first used.
